"Let's break this down step by step.\n\n1. **Monday**: Walt walked 4 miles.  \n   $$\n   \\text{Monday} = 4 \\text{ miles}\n   $$\n\n2. **Tuesday**: He walked 6 times as many miles as on Monday.  \n   $$\n   \\text{Tuesday} = 6 \\times 4 = 24 \\text{ miles}\n   $$\n\n3. **Total mileage from Monday to Wednesday**: 41 miles.  \n   $$\n   \\text{Total} = \\text{Monday} + \\text{Tuesday} + \\text{Wednesday} = 41\n   $$\n\n4. **Find Wednesday's mileage**:  \n   $$\n   \\text{Wednesday} = 41 - (\\text{Monday} + \\text{Tuesday}) = 41 - (4 + 24) = 41 - 28 = 13\n   $$\n\n**Answer: 13**"
